4.Change your app's main theme color (primarySwatch) in MaterialApp and use hot restart to see the effect. Note the difference between hot reload and hot restart
in how the change appears.


import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(MaterialApp(
    theme: ThemeData(
      primarySwatch: Colors.green,
    ),
    home: Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(
        title: const Text('Hello Flutter'),
      ),
      body: const Center(
        child: Text('Hello, Flutter!'),
      ),
    ),
  ));
}


Difference Between Hot Reload and Hot Restart:--

Hot Reload                                                              	Hot Restart

Updates the UI without restarting the app.	                         Restarts the entire app.
Preserves the current state.	                                       Resets the app state.
Faster than hot restart.	                                           Slower than hot reload.
Does not rerun main().	                                             Reruns main().
